  "lineage": "Colombian national rhythm and song-form in characteristic 6/8 meter with three-against-two syncopation — codified through the late-19th-century Andean Colombian school (Pedro Morales Pino, the bandola virtuoso who systematized the trio andino instrumentation), 20th-century anchors Garzón y Collazos (the post-WWII bambuco-trio voice, El Camino de la Vida 1951), Silva y Villalba, the modern Gustavo Adolfo Renjifo and Carranguero-tradition Jorge Velosa extensions; performed by the trio andino of tiple, bandola andina, and classical guitar with vocal duet or trio",
